rom afar  i'm so proud of what they're doing  speaking up  not giving giving up not never backing  down  the sense of community and how the  neighborhood residents just are coming  together  it's not a tenants versus landlord case  rather our we're fighting for our  right to exist to maintain living  in jerusalem a city where there's little  room left on which to build  and if palestinians leave they can lose  residency rights  we are both in the 70s  and to begin a new life in this age  it's not possible but on august 1st it's  likely  they will have little choice redmond  shannon global news  next what emerged when the water receded  an italian village is resurfacing for  the first time in over 70 years  it was once home to hundreds of people  before it flooded  as mike derlay reports it's almost like  a real life atlantis  pie up in northern italy tucked away in  an alpine postcard of a valley  sits the most curious of tourist  attractions a 14th century bell tower  rising above the cobalt blue waters  of lake asia the tiny village of quran  was put on the map  70 years ago when it disappeared against  the wishes of the town's people  italian authorities flooded the town to  make way for a hydroelectric plant  quran would become a curiosity for  divers  despite the low visibility in its waters  and when some writers were looking for a  locale for a horror tv show  quran fit the bill the lake has awakened  once again  the curse destroys everything hmm curse  eh  wonder what they say now that the  village has awakened  a few months ago the lake was drained  for maintenance leaving the town exposed  for the first time since 1950  yet because all the hotels are closed  due to covid nobody outside the region  seemed to notice  and only recently have visitors begun  looking around  steps probably were the entrance of a  house or a farmhouse  says this tourist canada has its own  quran  in alberta you can visit the resort town  of minnewanka landing  but you need scuba 